;. /technical_atlas_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition technical_atlas
  ;= Maintain an executable technical atlas

    This atlas connects concept documents to selected native definitions and
    an actual deterministic example step. It is not a mirror of README files.
    The catalogue binds the repository documents below through existing source
    hands. Missing documents are unavailable evidence, not empty manuals.

    Use Declared authoring actions, Inspect callable definitions, with inspection
    care x to inspect one
    compiler mirror entry or published callable's own record. Bind capture to
    the raw frozen inspection cell path, without /x. Select a narrow record;
    a collection snapshot is deliberately refused by this adapter. A capture
    remains pinned. Inspect and rebind deliberately to adopt a new definition.

    Choose the Nenex writer and a new destination; select an existing revision
    provider or edit its drafts manually. Source changes use the existing hand,
    cells, context overlays and holes. An example in prose is not a passed test.

    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= Selected manuals and native examples

    ;@ /flow/input capture
    ;= Exact native definition selected in an inspection cell

    ;@ /flow/step example ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/inventory
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Execute evidence validation and expose its result in the retained trace

    ;@ /flow/step grounded ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/captured_sources
    ;@ /flow/bind capture capture
    ;@ /flow/bind sources example
    ;= Bring the selected native definition alongside its documentation

    ;@ /flow/step concepts ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/revise
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Author evidence-bound concept documents

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages concepts
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Publish explanations with source provenance

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= A maintained technical tree

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses shrine grove nenex harness native
    ;= A working map of Shrine
      Explain how PLAN and Foil values, Grove interfaces, namespace records,
      cells, overlays, hands, Goo and Semidoc fit together. Give a reading path
      into the named children. Use the exact selected native definition as the
      worked anchor. Cite its native reference. State where the supplied manuals
      stop; do not invent an Enki runtime manual or imply complete coverage.

    ;@ /flow/page language_and_runtime
    ;@ /flow/uses shrine reflection native
    ;= Foil, PLAN, reflection and the runtime boundary
      Explain the language and runtime boundary supported by the supplied docs
      and reflection demo. Describe what the selected native value actually
      declares. Distinguish a type or decompiled law from execution evidence.
      Treat omitted or opaque portions of reflected display as unknown.

    ;@ /flow/page interfaces
    ;@ /flow/uses grove goo nenex native
    ;= Grove, Goo and document interfaces
      Explain contracts, views and declared controls, and how Semidoc and Goo
      preserve the same authored relationships. Show a short inert example
      grounded in the evidence. Refer to exact definitions, not guessed paths.

    ;@ /flow/page computation
    ;@ /flow/uses cell_examples hands overlays harness native
    ;= Cells, hands, overlays and executable examples
      Explain pure derived views, explicit effects and dependency-driven work.
      Use this atlas's inventory step as its executed example: the retained trace
      exposes the actual selected input and validated result. Other examples are
      illustrative until separately run. Explain how a person can embed another
      published flow occurrence using the existing Nenex controls, bind it, inspect
      its cells and resolve its holes. Do not claim arbitrary source code ran.
